<TrustPage title={`Privacy Policy — ${SITE_TITLE}`} description="What JayArr Coffee measures, what its tools keep on your own device, and which outside services the site uses: Google Analytics, Vercel, YouTube and Amazon." kicker="Legal" updated="October 19, 2026">
	<Fragment slot="title">Privacy <em>policy</em></Fragment>
	<p class="lede" slot="lede">JayArr Coffee ("we") runs jayarr.coffee. This page says what the site measures, what the tools keep in your browser, and which outside services are involved. There are no accounts, comments or newsletter, so the site never asks for your name or email address.</p>

	<h2>What we measure</h2>
	<p>Two page counters run on the site. Google Analytics runs only on jayarr.coffee itself, never on preview or local copies.</p>

	<h3>Google Analytics 4</h3>
	<ul>
		<li><strong>Page views.</strong> When a page loads, our setup sends Google the page's address, and the address of the page you came from, without their query strings (the part after "?", where the tools keep their settings).</li>
		<li><strong>Google's automatic measurement</strong> is switched on for this site, and it records more than that: when you scroll to the bottom of a page, file downloads, clicks on links to other sites with the full link address (for an Amazon search, the search words), and a new page view each time a tool rewrites the page's address as you change its settings. That address includes the settings, for example the two drinks you are comparing. It is also set to look for an email address, phone number or postal address typed into a form; no page here asks for any of them.</li>
		<li><strong>Our shop-link event.</strong> When you follow a link to a shop (Amazon, Nespresso or a maker's own site), the site sends an <code>outbound_click</code> event with only the shop's host name, such as amazon.com, and the path of the page you were on. It carries no query strings, nothing you entered in a tool and no search text, and it is sent only from jayarr.coffee.</li>
		<li><strong>Cookies and IP addresses.</strong> Google Analytics sets its own cookies (<code>_ga</code>) to tell visits apart. Google says Google Analytics 4 does not log or store IP addresses.</li>
		<li><strong>Opting out.</strong> Install the <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google Analytics opt-out browser add-on</a>, or block cookies or scripts for this site in your browser. See <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google's privacy policy</a>.</li>
	</ul>

	<h3>Vercel Web Analytics</h3>
	<p>Vercel hosts the site, and its Web Analytics script (<code>/_vercel/insights/script.js</code>) counts page views. According to <a href="https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/privacy-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Vercel's documentation</a>:</p>
	<ul>
		<li>it uses no cookies; a visit is told apart by a hash made from the incoming request, and the hash is discarded after 24 hours;</li>
		<li>each page view records the time, the page's address, the site you came from, a rough location (country, region and city), your operating system and browser with their versions, and the device type;</li>
		<li>it collects no personal identifiers, and the figures are used in aggregate.</li>
	</ul>
	<p>Our setup removes the query string and the part after "#" from the address before Vercel records it, so the tool settings in a shared link, such as a Brew Guide recipe or a caffeine day, aren't part of it. The address of the page you came from is recorded as your browser sends it, and when you move from one page of this site to another, that can include the settings in the previous page's address.</p>

	<h2>What the tools keep in your browser</h2>
	<p>The site sets no cookies of its own. Tools that remember things keep them in your browser's local storage, on this device only. None of it is sent to us, and we can't see it:</p>
	<ul>
		<li><strong>Brew Guide:</strong> the recipes you save and your last brew.</li>
		<li><strong>Caffeine:</strong> your drink diary and its settings (half-life, bedtime and the pregnancy setting).</li>
		<li><strong>Freshness:</strong> the details of your last bag.</li>
		<li><strong>Flavor Bloom:</strong> your tasting card and the cards you keep.</li>
		<li><strong>Nespresso pods:</strong> your machine's line and your tasting flight.</li>
		<li><strong>Grind Calibrator:</strong> your grinder.</li>
	</ul>
	<p>The tools page reads these to show what you've saved. The homepage remembers which starting point you chose for as long as the tab is open. Clearing this site's data in your browser removes all of it. If your browser blocks storage, the tools still work but keep nothing after you leave.</p>
	<p><strong>The caffeine diary's pregnancy setting stays on your device.</strong> A caffeine share link leaves it out, along with your half-life, since a slow half-life could hint at it: the link carries only the drinks and your bedtime.</p>

	<h2>Share links and search</h2>
	<p>A share link is only made when you press a tool's Share or Copy button. It carries that tool's settings in its address, so anyone you send it to sees them, and opening it is counted as described above. Site search runs in your browser against an index downloaded from this site; what you type in the search box isn't sent to either counter and isn't put in the page's address.</p>

	<h2>Videos</h2>
	<p>Videos show a thumbnail image from YouTube's image server. The YouTube player, and YouTube's cookies with it, loads only when you press play. YouTube is covered by <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google's privacy policy</a>.</p>

	<h2>Affiliate and shop links</h2>
	<p>Some links are Amazon affiliate links (see the <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">affiliate disclosure</a>). Once you follow a link to Amazon, Nespresso or a maker's site, that site's own privacy policy and cookies apply.</p>

	<h2>Data retention</h2>
	<p>Google Analytics keeps event-level data for 2 months and user-level data for 14 months, after which Google deletes it automatically; its summary reports aren't affected. Vercel discards the visitor hash after 24 hours.</p>

	<h2>Your choices</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>Opt out of Google Analytics with the add-on above, or block cookies or scripts for this site.</li>
		<li>Clear this site's data in your browser to remove anything the tools saved.</li>
		<li>Ask us to delete any personal data we hold, at the address below.</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>Children's privacy</h2>
	<p>The site is not directed at children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect personal information from children.</p>

	<h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
	<p>We'll post any change on this page with a new date at the top.</p>

	<h2>Contact</h2>
	<p>Questions about privacy: <a href="mailto:jay@jayarr.coffee">jay@jayarr.coffee</a>.</p>
</TrustPage>
